<title>USA: Paxson Communications to issue shares - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Paxson Communications to issue shares - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paxson Communications Corp is expected to sell $150 million in 10-year cumulative exchangeable preferred shares this week, the Wall Street Journal reported Monday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the issue, non-callable for five years, will be exchangeable into senior subordinated debt and carry a coupon.</p>
<p>During the first six years, the radio and television station operator will have the option to pay in kind, which means paying investors more shares instead of cash, it said.</p>
